#BIG BENCH 
#Author:Aarohi Srivastava 
#Year:2022
#Summary:
BIG-bench is a benchmark used to test how smart Large Language Models (LLMs) are by giving them many difficult tasks like reasoning, math, coding, and language
understanding. It was created because older benchmarks had become too easy for modern AI models. The research showed that as AI models become larger, they can 
suddenly develop new abilities and perform much better on complex tasks.
#Method:
It was tested by whole community by difficult taks orginaaly 200 but due to high cost 24 very difficult tasks on diffrent subjects
#DATASET:
Model     	           Performance on BIG-bench
GPT-2	                 Low performance; struggled on most reasoning tasks.
GPT-3                  (smaller versions)	Moderate performance; solved basic tasks but failed on many complex ones.
GPT-3                  (175B)	High performance; showed strong reasoning and emergent abilities on several tasks.
Other large models     (e.g., PaLM, later evaluations)	Performed even better than GPT-3 on many BIG-bench tasks as model size increased.
Intersting ideas:
-Emergent Abilities – Large AI models can suddenly learn new skills (like solving logic puzzles or complex reasoning) once they reach a certain size,
instead of improving gradually.
-Community-Driven Benchmark – Hundreds of researchers contributed tasks, making the benchmark more diverse and reducing bias from a single research group.
Limitations:
-IT was computational expensive
-Some tasks may become outdated as models improve
